  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A helicopter takes off from the ground and travels vertically upwards at a constant speed of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. After the helicopter has been traveling for <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8.0\"></span> seconds, a stone is dropped from the helicopter. Assuming that air resistance is negligible, what is the best estimate for the time it takes for the stone to reach the ground?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{32}\"></span> s</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6\"></span> s</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{56}\"></span> s</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"8\"></span> s</li>\n</ol>"
